# Example 29: ML-guided directed evolution of GB1 (S8)
# Python companion script: examples/directed_evolution_workflow.py
# Closed-loop "design-build-test-learn" protein engineering in miniature,
# mirroring EVOLVEpro (Jiang et al. Science 2025 387:eadr6006),
# MULTI-evolve (Tran et al. Science 2025 388:aea1820) and FSFP
# (Otalora Ottó et al. Nat Commun 2024 15:5566):
#
#   landscape = weighted-BLOSUM62 chemical-tolerance model of the GB1
#               IgG-binding domain (56 residues), interface window
#               (residues 39-54, Wu et al. 2016 Nature 532:58) weighted
#               harder; identity = 1.0.
#   oracle    = zero-shot predictor scored against the wild type:
#               ESM-2 pseudo-likelihood (Frazer et al. 2021) when
#               transformers/torch are installed, else BLOSUM62.
#   loop      = cripple the wild type -> per round: mutate the best
#               variant, rank the library with the oracle, screen the
#               top-K on the landscape, promote the best screen hit.
#
# The guided campaign recovers far more fitness than an oracle-free
# random-screening baseline, and the oracle's round-1 predictions align
# with the landscape (Spearman, the ProteinGym benchmark metric).
#
#gene name=gb1_domain
ATG GCT GGT GTA TAA
#end
#
#config ticks=100 output=stdout
